From 856128cb4c19feb629986a9c738d509e558bbafb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HelaFaye <dilsha21@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 14:06:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] power-domain: board parts on a switched supply

A power-domain lists parts by id (devices=lcd:touch) and is switched by its
'on' property (qom-set at run time) or, with switched=on, by its 'enable'
line through a pin-link (a regulator's enable driven by the firmware, as the
T-Deck's BOARD_POWERON). Off, its SSI and I2C parts drop off their buses (an
unpowered flag the SSI and I2C cores skip: no ACK, nothing on MISO); on again,
each is cold-reset, as a part coming up from no supply. Tests: an MCP23017
that NACKs and comes back with its reset values, one switched by GPIO10, and
an ILI9341 that reads no ID and comes back asleep.
---
